   "en": "<figure class=\"image\">\n <img alt=\"Filing Taxes in Taiwan: A Quick Guide for Expats\" sizes=\"100vw\" src=\"https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_EEH1WE9.jpg\" srcset=\"https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_oiM0I0j.jpg 800w, https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_K7TKiJW.jpg 1024w, https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_zV1omv2.jpg 1920w\" width=\"1920\"/>\n</figure>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n  In Taiwan, tax season runs from\n  <strong>\n   May 1 to May 31\n  </strong>\n  each year. For expats living and working here, filing taxes for the first time can feel confusing or overwhelming. Whether you're employed by a local company or earning income from abroad, understanding your tax responsibilities is key. This guide breaks down the essential questions to ease the process:\n </span>\n <br/>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>\n <br/>\n</p>\n<ol>\n <li>\n  <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n   <strong>\n    Do foreigners need to file taxes in Taiwan?\n   </strong>\n  </span>\n  <br/>\n  <br/>\n  <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n   Yes. If y",
   "zh": "<p>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"image\">\n <img alt=\"台灣報稅簡易指南\" sizes=\"100vw\" src=\"https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_tPTCyFa.jpg\" srcset=\"https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_JBQ2wtD.jpg 800w, https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_J7Xk3E0.jpg 1024w, https://storage.talent.nat.gov.tw/media/articles/images/tax-pay-flat-collage-with-finance-bills-receipts-vector-illustration_982_lQLe0v9.jpg 1920w\" width=\"1920\"/>\n</figure>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n  在台灣，一年一度的報稅季為每年\n  <strong>\n   5 月 1 日至 5 月 31 日\n  </strong>\n  。對於居住並在台工作的外籍人士來說，首次報稅可能會感到困惑或壓力大。然而，無論您是受僱於台灣公司，或是從海外賺取收入，了解自己的納稅義務都是相當重要的。本文統整了以下關鍵問題，協助您更順利地完成報稅流程：\n </span>\n</p>\n<p>\n <br/>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n  <strong>\n   一、外國人也要報稅嗎？\n  </strong>\n </span>\n <br/>\n <br/>\n 是的\n <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n  。只要外籍人士在台有賺取收入，就需要依照規定納稅。課稅方式會根據當年度「在台居留日數」而有所不同。\n </span>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n</p>\n<p>\n <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n  <strong>\n   二、課稅方式一覽\n  </strong>\n </span>\n <br/>\n <br/>\n <span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">\n  依據居留日數分為「居住者」與「非居"
  },
